1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nulji Maripgan (訥祗 麻立干, ?-458, reigned 417-458) was the 19th king of Silla and the first king to use the title of maripgan according to the Samguk Sagi. To quote Kim Dae-moon in the Shilla Bongi, “Maripgan is a dia
2 CONC lect that refers to stakes. A stake refers to a hamjo, and it is placed according to the official authority. In other words, he spread the stakes of the servants under it, mainly the stakes of the king, so this is how he named the
2 CONC  king.”
2 CONT
2 CONT In 392, the 37th year of his reign, Naemul Isageum sent Silseong to Goguryeo as a hostage, and Silseong was furious and drove out Naemul's son Nulji and sent his younger brothers Bokho and Misaheon as hostages to Goguryeo and Wa, 
2 CONC respectively. After that, the Goguryeo people tried to kill Nulji, but Nulji assassinated Silseong and ascended the throne. Bok-ho and Mi Sa-heon ordered Park Je-sang to return in 418, and this anecdote is recorded in detail in th
2 CONC e Samguk Yusa.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 424, in February of the lunar calendar, an envoy was sent to Goguryeo. In April 431 of the lunar calendar, the Japanese invaded the east and surrounded Myeongseonghwa, but withdrew without any income. In the spring of 432 there
2 CONC  was a famine. In 433, Mi Sa-hun died, and the king paid a tribute to Seo Bul-han. He made peace with Baekje in the 7th month of the lunar calendar that year (I-I alliance). The relationship between me and I improved, so in 434, K
2 CONC ing Yuu sent two horses in February of the lunar calendar, a white hawk in September of the lunar calendar, and in October of the lunar calendar, Nulji sent gold and silk in return.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 440, the Japanese invaded the southern and eastern borders twice and kidnapped the people. In the 4th month of the lunar calendar in 444, the Japanese attacked on a larger scale and surrounded Venus for 10 days, but ran out of 
2 CONC supplies and fled. The king pursued with thousands of cavalry and fought east of Doksan, but more than half of the Silla soldiers were killed. When the king was defeated, he abandoned his horse and climbed up the mountain, surroun
2 CONC ded by several layers of enemies, but the fog was thick and he could barely escape from the eyes of the Japanese.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 7th month of the lunar year of the 450th year, a general of Goguryeo was hunting in the field of Siljik, and Hasla Seongju Samjik killed him. King Jangsu raised an angry army, but withdrew after Maripgan apologized. However
2 CONC , Goguryeo invaded again in August of the lunar calendar in 454, and in October of 455 by the lunar calendar, Goguryeo invaded Baekje by sending troops to rescue them.
