1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 3 FEB 479
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jabi Maripgan (慈悲 麻立干, ? - March 12, 479 (February 3, lunar calendar); reigned 458 - March 12, 479) was the 20th king of Silla. He is the eldest son of Nulji Maripgan and the grandson of Shilseong Isa-geum. Queen K
2 CONC im was the daughter of Mi Sa-heon, who was a Buddhist, and was married to her in 461, the fourth year of his reign.
2 CONT
2 CONT In April of the lunar calendar in 459, the Japanese attacked with more than 100 military ships and surrounded Wolseong. Over half of the Silla army guarded the fortress under the command of Maripgan, waited for the enemy to retrea
2 CONC t, chased them, and drove them to the mouth of the sea, causing them to drown and die. In the 5th month of the lunar calendar, in 462, the Japanese invaded again, occupied Whalgaeseong, and captured more than 1,000 people. The fol
2 CONC lowing year, in February of the 463 lunar calendar, they attacked again and attacked Sapryangseong, but failed. Maripgan ordered Bulji and Deokji to ambush the Japanese soldiers and defeated them greatly. In this year, two castles
2 CONC  were built on the frontier to prevent Japanese invasions, and the army was inspected in the 7th month of the lunar calendar, and the battleship was repaired in 467.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the spring of 468, Goguryeo and Malgal attacked Siljik. In the ninth month of the lunar calendar, people over the age of 15 were recruited from Hasla residents and built a castle in Haeae. Afterwards, Maripgan focused on establ
2 CONC ishing the defense system and toured the entire Silla region in July of the lunar calendar to recover from flood damage in April of the lunar calendar in 469, built Samnyeonsanseong in 470, Moroseong in 471, and repaired Myeongseo
2 CONC ngseong in 473. In 474 AD, castles such as Ilmo, Sashi, Gwangseok, Dapdal, Gurye, and Jura were built.
2 CONT
2 CONT When King Jangsu of Goguryeo attacked Baekje in the 7th month of the lunar calendar in 475, King Gaero sent his crown prince Munju to ask for salvation. Maripgan sent reinforcements to Baekje. This event is recorded as 474 in the 
2 CONC Silla Bongi, but both are recorded as 475 in the Goguryeo and Baekje Bonki, so the record of the Silla Bongi is considered to be incorrect.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 476, when the Japanese invaded the east in June of the lunar calendar, Maripgan ordered Deokji to repel it, killing 200 people and capturing them. In 477, in the 5th month of the lunar calendar, he raised an army again and atta
2 CONC cked it in five branches, but returned without any income.
