1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wu_Zetian  Empress Wu Zetian] Wu Zetian (simplified Chinese: 武则天; traditional Chinese: 武則天; pinyin: Wǔ Zétiān) (17 February[citation needed] 624[10][12] – 16 December 705[11]), persona
2 CONC l name Wu Zhao (武曌), often referred to as Tian Hou (天后) during Tang Dynasty and Empress Consort Wu (武后) in later times, was the only woman in the history of China to assume the title of Empress Regnant. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As de facto ruler of China first through her husband and her sons from 665 to 690, not unprecedented in Chinese history, she then broke all precedents when she founded her own dynasty in 690, the Zhou (周) (interrupting the Tang Dy
2 CONC nasty), and ruled personally under the name Sacred and Divine Empress Regnant (聖神皇帝) and variations thereof from 690 to 705. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.archive.org/details/empresswu   1939 free movie download]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=194389 '''Wu Zhao''' 武曌] cf. 補遺 7:138-139; 文物 1999.1:93; 洛陽新獲續 504 . Death year estimated by Tackett (cc659) — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
