1 NAME Kut Chor
2 GIVN Kut Chor
2 NICK Kül-chor
2 NICK (Old Turkic: Küli Čur)
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 TITL Turgesh Khagan
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BCrgesh
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kut_Chor
2 CONT
2 CONT Kut Chor (Chinese: 骨啜; pinyin: Gǔchuài; full title: Chinese: 吐火仙骨啜可汗; pinyin: Tǔhuǒxiāngǔchuài Kèhán) — was a son of Suluk and briefly served as Turgesh khagan.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Reign He was set up on throne by Tumodu in Suyab, having support of the Black Turgesh and his brother Ton Apa Yabgu. His main contenders were Baga Tarkhan and Erwei Tegin in Taraz.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 27 August 739, Baga Tarkhan allied with Tang general Gai Jiayun (蓋嘉運), King of Chach Baghatur Tudun (莫賀咄吐屯) and attacked Kut Chor. He was sent to Changan, where he was symbolically sacrificed before imperial temple only to be p
2 CONC ardoned by Xuanzong and created a Tang general in Left Guard.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT  1912-1992., Gumilev, L. N. (Lev Nikolaevich) (2002). Drevnie ti︠u︡rki. Sankt-Peterburg: SZKĖO "KRISTALL". ISBN 9785950300318. OCLC 319803222.
2 CONT  Quan Tang wen, vol 24. Dong, Gao, 1740-1818., 董誥, 1740-1818. (Di 1 ban ed.). Beijing: Zhonghua shu ju. 1983. ISBN 7101007163. OCLC 20575264. Sources Old Book of Tang, vol 144
